    #}
    <div class="hero__collage" aria-hidden="true">
      {% image "/assets/images/hero-collage.png", "", {
        sizes: "(min-width: 800px) 50vw, 100vw",
        formats: ["webp", "png"],
        loading: "eager",
        fetchpriority: "high"
      } %}
    </div>

  </div>

  <img class="hero__tear" src="/assets/images/torn-paper.png" alt="" aria-hidden="true">
</section>


{# ======================================================== #}
{# FIELD GUIDE INTRO                                         #}
{# ======================================================== #}
<section class="field-guide-intro">
  <div class="wrap field-guide-intro__inner">
    <div class="field-guide-intro__lead">
      <p class="eyebrow">What Brooke Reports Helps You See</p>
      <h2>Modern life is persuasive. That doesn't mean you have to be easy to steer.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="field-guide-intro__copy">
      <p>Every day, you're surrounded by messages trying to move you. Buy this. Believe this. Hurry up. Trust me. Fix yourself. Don't miss out. Everyone else is already ahead.</p>
      <p>Most of it isn't evil. Most of it isn't even hidden. It's just designed.</p>
      <p>Brooke Reports helps you notice how persuasion works in marketing, media, business advice, online offers, social platforms, and everyday decision-making; so you can separate the signal from the pressure.</p>
      <p class="field-guide-intro__punch">Persuasion literacy for people who want to stay curious without getting played.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


{# ======================================================== #}
{# FEATURED REPORTS                                          #}
{# ======================================================== #}
<section class="featured-reports">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="featured-reports__header">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Latest Field Notes</p>
        <h2 class="featured-reports__heading">Fresh clues.<br>Clearer choices.</h2>
      </div>
      <a href="/blog/" class="featured-reports__all">Read all reports <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
    </div>

    <div class="featured-reports__grid">
      {% for post in collections.posts | limit(4) %}
      <article class="report-card">

        <div class="report-card__image">
          {% if post.data.image %}
          {% image post.data.image, post.data.imageAlt or post.data.title, {
            sizes: "(min-width: 900px) 280px, (min-width: 580px) 50vw, 100vw",
            widths: [280, 560]
          } %}
          {% else %}
          <div class="report-card__placeholder" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          {% endif %}
        </div>

        <div class="report-card__body">
          {% if post.data.category %}
          <p class="eyebrow report-card__eyebrow">{{ post.data.category }}</p>
          {% endif %}
          <h3 class="report-card__title">
            <a href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.title }}</a>
          </h3>
          {% if post.data.description %}
          <p class="report-card__excerpt">{{ post.data.description }}</p>
          {% endif %}
          <footer class="report-card__meta">
            <time datetime="{{ post.date | htmlDateString }}">{{ post.date | readableDate }}</time>
            {% if post.data.readTime %}
            <span aria-hidden="true"> &middot; </span><span>{{ post.data.readTime }} min read</span>
            {% endif %}
          </footer>
        </div>

      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


{# ======================================================== #}
{# CASES WE TAKE                                             #}
{# ======================================================== #}
<section class="cases-we-take">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="cases-we-take__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">What We Investigate</p>
      <h2>Cases We Take</h2>
      <p>Not murders. Not conspiracy boards. Just the everyday confusion that shows up wearing a polished headline and very confident claims.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cases-we-take__grid">
      <article class="case-card">
        <p class="case-card__label">Case 01</p>
        <h3>Persuasive Marketing</h3>
        <p>Sales pages, offers, testimonials, urgency, authority signals, vague promises, and shiny claims that may or may not contain actual evidence.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="case-card">
        <p class="case-card__label">Case 02</p>
        <h3>Attention Traps</h3>
        <p>The feeds, apps, notifications, trends, and tiny design choices that tax your focus before you've even had coffee.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="case-card">
        <p class="case-card__label">Case 03</p>
        <h3>Social Pressure</h3>
        <p>The group norms, status signals, identity cues, and invisible &ldquo;everyone's doing this&rdquo; energy that can make a decision feel obvious when it's not.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="case-card">
        <p class="case-card__label">Case 04</p>
        <h3>Business Advice &amp; Internet Hype</h3>
        <p>Frameworks, gurus, creator economy promises, productivity claims, and advice that sounds smart until you ask, &ldquo;For whom? Under what conditions?&rdquo;</p>
      </article>

      <article class="case-card">
        <p class="case-card__label">Case 05</p>
        <h3>Human Behavior</h3>
        <p>Cognitive biases, emotional framing, decision fatigue, incentives, body language, and the ordinary human patterns that make smart people surprisingly persuadable.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


